\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now All The Woods Are Sleeping,
\par And night and stillness creeping
\par O'er city, man and beast;
\par But thou, my heart, awake thee,
\par To prayer awhile betake thee,
\par And praise thy Maker ere thou rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The last faint beam is going,
\par The golden stars are glowing
\par In yonder dark-blue deep;
\par And such the glory given
\par When called of God to heaven,
\par On earth no more we pine and weep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Now thought and labour ceases,
\par For night the tired releases,
\par And bids sweet rest begin:
\par My heart, there comes a morrow
\par Shall set thee free from sorrow,
\par And all the dreary toil of sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My Jesus, stay Thou by me,
\par And let no foe come nigh me,
\par Safe shelter by Thy wing;
\par But would the foe alarm me,
\par O let him never harm me,
\par But still Thine angels round me sing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. My loved ones, rest securely,
\par From evil peril surely
\par Our God will guard your heads;
\par And happy slumbers send you,
\par And bid His hosts attend you,
\par And golden- armed watch o'er your beds.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

